+{"branch":"direct_complete_proof","status":"screened","reasoning":"Upper bound: at a fixed vertex, among five incident red/blue edges at least three share a color. Their other endpoints either contain an edge of that color, completing a triangle through the fixed vertex, or all three mutual edges have the opposite color, completing a triangle among them. Lower bound: on residues modulo 5, color pairs at difference plus or minus 1 red and pairs at difference plus or minus 2 blue. A putative monochromatic triangle through a vertex would have its other two vertices equal to the two same-color neighbors; those two are joined in the opposite color. Thus neither color has a triangle. The two parts give R(3,3) at most 6 and greater than 5, hence exactly 6."}
